    "text": "Gawain is one of the best known knights of the Round Table. Other names are Gawayne, Gavin, Gauvain, and Gwalchmei. He served king Arthur. He was Arthur's nephew, the son of Morgause and king Lot of Orkney. He was one of Arthur's first supporters. He is the hero of Sir Gawain and the Green Knight. The poem dates to about 1370 CE. The Pearl Poet wrote it. Gawain beheaded the Green Knight. The knight returned exactly one year later. The host's wife, Bercilak's wife, tried to seduce the chaste Gawain three times. She left her girdle with him. Gawain hid it instead of returning it. The Green Knight then struck three times. The third blow wounded him for hiding the girdle. Some scholars read Gawain as a late version of the smith god Goibniu. The Green Knight may echo the Green Man.",
